  "result": "Perfect! All 96 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT support for the invoicing system. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- Imported `roundCents` from money.js\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to calculate VAT:\n  - VAT is computed per line on the line's amount **after discount**\n  - Each line's VAT is rounded individually using `roundCents()` (banker's rounding)\n  - Invoice VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs\n  - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` where `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n**src/render.js**\n- Imported `invoiceTotals` from invoices.js\n- Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to display:\n  - Subtotal\n  - Discount (only shown if non-zero)\n  - VAT (only shown if non-zero)\n  - Total (displayed just above the VAT line)\n\n**test/invoices.test.js**\n- Imported `roundCents` for consistent VAT rounding in tests\n- Added 5 new tests for VAT calculation:\n  - VAT on amount after discount\n  - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n  - VAT-exempt products (vatRate 0)\n  - Total calculation formula: subtotal - discount + vat\n- Updated 5 existing tests to account for VAT in totals\n\n**test/render.test.js**\n- Updated 2 existing tests to check for the new summary lines\n- Added 4 new tests:\n  - Verifying subtotal, discount, VAT, and total appear\n  - Testing conditional display (discount/VAT only shown when non-zero)\n  - Verifying VAT line appears above total line\n\nThe implementation follows proper invoice accounting practices: VAT is calculated per line after discount and clamped at 0, with banker's rounding applied to each line's VAT before summing.",
